[PARTIAL LOG: the exe terminated silently a few seconds after printing FUSEOPT_PLM
(user report: process died, host unaffected - an access violation on unmapped user
VA, not a bus stall; the earlier "machine freeze" reading was wrong). Root cause
(tool bug, fixed same day): the turing shifted-bank section subtracted 0x7FF000
from the two PRI-ring rows (0x120060/0x1200A0) which are NOT option-bank rows;
0x120060 - 0x7FF000 underflowed u32, the release build wrapped silently, and the
read landed ~4 GiB past the 16 MiB user mapping. Read-only round: no writes
occurred. The re-run with the fixed build completed normally: see
ssdiag-v074-ga100vfi-full.log.]
